---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Sarthak Bichhawa — Sr. Data & Applied Scientist · Microsoft
desc: "The case for hiring Sarthak Bichhawa: nine years of production ML and AI — autonomous multi-agent LLM systems, a fleet-scale embedding platform, and the revenue systems behind $5B+/year. Claims up front, receipts attached."
---

<!-- ============================================================
     HERO — profile + impact, nothing between them.
     Deliberately NOT .reveal: this is the LCP element and must not
     wait on JavaScript to become visible.
     ============================================================ -->
<header class="hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="hero-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="hero-no"><span class="no">Passionate about data.</span></p>
        <h1>The case for<br>hiring <em>Sarthak.</em></h1>
        <p class="hero-lead">{{ facts.summary.hero }}</p>
        <p class="hero-meta">
          <b class="seg">{{ facts.identity.title }}</b> <span class="sep">·</span> <span class="seg">{{ facts.identity.org }}, {{ facts.identity.team }}</span>
          <span class="sep">·</span> <span class="seg">since {{ facts.identity.tenure_start }}</span> <span class="sep">·</span> <span class="seg">{{ facts.identity.location }}</span><br>
          <span class="seg scope">{{ facts.identity.scope_short }}</span><br>
          <span class="open"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>OPEN TO: {{ facts.identity.open_to | join(" · ") }}</span>
        </p>
        <div class="hero-ctas">
          <a href="mailto:{{ facts.identity.email }}" class="btn btn-primary" data-goatcounter-click="hero-email">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 4h16c1.1 0 2 .9 2 2v12c0 1.1-.9 2-2 2H4c-1.1 0-2-.9-2-2V6c0-1.1.9-2 2-2z"/><polyline points="22,6 12,13 2,6"/></svg>
            Email me
          </a>
          <a href="/resume/" class="btn btn-ghost" data-goatcounter-click="hero-resume">Résumé</a>
          <button class="btn btn-mono copy-btn" type="button" data-goatcounter-click="hero-copy-summary">⧉ copy candidate summary</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <img class="hero-photo" src="/assets/sarthak.jpg" alt="Sarthak Bichhawa" width="232" height="232" fetchpriority="high" />
    </div>

    <!-- the headline receipts -->
    <div id="receipts">
      <div class="receipts panel">
        {%- for r in facts.receipts %}
        <a class="receipt" href="{{ r.anchor }}">
          <span class="r-ref">receipt → {{ r.anchor }}</span>
          <span class="r-val">{{ r.value }}</span>
          <span class="r-lbl">{{ r.label }}</span>
          <span class="r-sub">{{ r.sub }}</span>
        </a>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
      <p class="mono-note strip-note">// every number on this page links to its receipt. <span class="g">click through.</span></p>
    </div>

    <!-- sixty-second path, for the reader who arrived from the résumé -->
    <nav class="quickpath reveal" aria-label="Sixty-second path">
      <span class="qp-label">Sixty seconds?</span>
      <a href="/case/incident-agent/">The flagship agent</a>
      <a href="/case/revenue-attribution/">The one that went wrong</a>
      <a href="#ask">Talk to me</a>
    </nav>
  </div>
</header>

<!-- ============================================================
     §01 — SYSTEMS LEDGER (+ lane selector)
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="section-pad" id="ledger" style="padding-top:3.25rem;">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="sec-mark">§01 — Systems on the record</div>
      <h2 class="sec-title">What runs in production, with proof.</h2>
      <p class="sec-sub">
        Not prototypes, not weekend demos — systems running inside Microsoft Azure
        Storage with users, on-call rotations, and numbers attached.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="lanes reveal" id="lanes" data-lanes-ui>
      <span class="lane-label">Hiring for</span>
      <div class="lane-btns" role="group" aria-label="Filter the record by discipline">
        {%- for l in facts.lanes %}
        <button type="button" class="lane-btn{{ ' on' if loop.first }}" data-lane="{{ l.id }}" data-blurb="{{ l.blurb }}" aria-pressed="{{ 'true' if loop.first else 'false' }}" data-goatcounter-click="lane-{{ l.id }}">{{ l.label }}</button>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
      <p class="lane-blurb mono-note" id="laneBlurb" aria-live="polite">// {{ facts.lanes[0].blurb }}</p>
    </div>

    <div class="board panel reveal">
      <div class="board-head">
        <span>ID</span><span>System</span><span>What it does</span><span>Proof</span><span>Status</span>
      </div>
      {%- for row in facts.systems %}
      <div class="board-row" data-lanes="{{ row.lanes | join(' ') }}">
        <span class="b-id">{{ row.id }}</span>
        <span class="b-name"><a href="{{ row.link }}">{{ row.name }}</a></span>
        <span class="b-desc">{{ row.what }}</span>
        <span class="b-proof">{{ row.proof }}</span>
        <span class="b-status {{ 'live' if row.status == 'LIVE' else 'prod' }}"><i aria-hidden="true"></i>{{ row.status }}</span>
      </div>
      {%- endfor %}
      <div class="board-foot">// side projects don't get a row. <span class="g">everything above ran in production with users who could file incidents.</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<hr class="rule"/>

<!-- ============================================================
     §02 — THE EXHIBITS
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="section-pad" id="exhibits">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="sec-mark">§02 — The exhibits</div>
      <h2 class="sec-title flip">The work, <em>architecture attached.</em></h2>
      <p class="sec-sub">
        Each exhibit opens into a full case file — planner design, prompts, eval
        output, the parts a hiring loop actually wants to inspect. Six systems,
        one of which is the one that went wrong.
      </p>
    </div>

    {%- for c in facts.cases %}
    <article class="exhibit" id="{{ c.id }}" data-lanes="{{ c.lanes | join(' ') }}">
      <div class="reveal">
        <div class="exhibit-tag">{{ c.tag }}</div>
        <h3 class="case-title">{{ c.title }}</h3>
        <p class="case-lede">{{ c.tease }}</p>
      </div>
      {%- if c.id == "exhibit-incident" %}{% include "partials/diagram-incident.njk" %}{% endif %}
      {%- if c.id == "exhibit-health" %}{% include "partials/diagram-mcc.njk" %}{% endif %}
      {%- if c.id == "exhibit-a2v" %}{% include "partials/diagram-a2v.njk" %}{% endif %}
      {%- if c.id == "exhibit-attribution" %}
      <div class="metric-row panel reveal">
        <div class="m"><span class="v">$5B+/yr</span><span class="d">platform revenue the attribution covers</span></div>
        <div class="m"><span class="v">20+</span><span class="d">pipeline components the failure hid inside</span></div>
        <div class="m"><span class="v">7</span><span class="d">incidents worked, one a 4-team severity-2</span></div>
        <div class="m"><span class="v">&lt;1%</span><span class="d">variance vs Finance, independently reconciled</span></div>
      </div>
      {%- endif %}
      {%- if c.id == "exhibit-trust" %}
      <div class="metric-row panel reveal">
        <div class="m"><span class="v">400+</span><span class="d">production datasets profiled hourly</span></div>
        <div class="m"><span class="v">~88%</span><span class="d">silent row loss caught before financial reports</span></div>
        <div class="m"><span class="v">99%</span><span class="d">throttling incidents eliminated, top customers</span></div>
        <div class="m"><span class="v">LLM</span><span class="d">lineage engine that reads pipeline code</span></div>
      </div>
      {%- endif %}
      {%- if c.id == "exhibit-stress" %}
      <div class="metric-row panel reveal">
        <div class="m"><span class="v">20</span><span class="d">workload types stress-tested per build</span></div>
        <div class="m"><span class="v">~500</span><span class="d">failure signals distilled</span></div>
        <div class="m"><span class="v">15</span><span class="d">recurring failure modes named</span></div>
        <div class="m"><span class="v">−40%</span><span class="d">test-infrastructure cost after bandit scheduling</span></div>
      </div>
      {%- endif %}
      <a href="{{ c.slug }}" class="case-cta panel reveal">
        <span>{{ c.scent }}</span>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/><polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19"/></svg>
      </a>
    </article>
    {%- endfor %}
    <p class="mono-note lane-empty" id="laneEmpty" hidden>// nothing in the record filed under that discipline. <span class="g">try “Everything”.</span></p>
  </div>
</section>

<hr class="rule"/>

<!-- ============================================================
     §03 — JUDGMENT CALLS
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="section-pad" id="judgment">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="sec-mark">§03 — Judgment</div>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Five calls I'd defend <em>in the interview.</em></h2>
      <p class="sec-sub">
        Senior hires aren't judged on tools — they're judged on decisions under
        ambiguity. Here are five of mine, with the trade-off and the outcome. Each
        comes with the question you should grill me on.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="calls-grid">
      <article class="call panel reveal" data-lanes="ai">
        <div class="call-kicker"><span>Call 01</span><span class="dom">architecture</span></div>
        <h3 class="call-title">{{ facts.judgment[0].title }}.</h3>
        <p class="call-body">
          The incident agent started on LangChain / LangGraph. Debugging through five layers of someone else's abstraction was slower than owning the loop — so I <strong>replaced it with a hand-rolled planner / executor</strong>: full LLM tracing, 429-storm retry, context compaction we control, concurrent tool dispatch.
        </p>
        <p class="call-out">→ faster iteration, traceable failures, an agent on-call actually trusts</p>
        <p class="call-ask"><b>ASK ME ABOUT:</b> {{ facts.judgment[0].ask_me_about }}</p>
      </article>

      <article class="call panel reveal" data-lanes="ai analytics">
        <div class="call-kicker"><span>Call 02</span><span class="dom">quality</span></div>
        <h3 class="call-title">{{ facts.judgment[1].title }}.</h3>
        <p class="call-body">
          The customer-health agent didn't meet a single real user until a <strong>golden-set eval harness, guardrails, and PII-aware prompts</strong> existed. Demos earn applause; evals earn production. The harness now gates every prompt and model change like CI.
        </p>
        <p class="call-out">→ 8+ teams on one surface, leadership quoting its numbers unprompted</p>
        <p class="call-ask"><b>ASK ME ABOUT:</b> {{ facts.judgment[1].ask_me_about }}</p>
      </article>

      <article class="call panel reveal" data-lanes="ai platform">
        <div class="call-kicker"><span>Call 03</span><span class="dom">platform</span></div>
        <h3 class="call-title">{{ facts.judgment[2].title }}.</h3>
        <p class="call-body">
          The account embeddings could have shipped as one team's similarity model. Instead I <strong>named the abstraction, wrote the design doc, and built the drift / coverage / staleness plumbing</strong> that makes other teams safe to depend on it — account, subscription, and customer tiers included. It's productionizing now with its first consumer, and the platform work is why the second one won't need me.
        </p>
        <p class="call-out">→ one representation, designed for reuse before reuse was demanded</p>
        <p class="call-ask"><b>ASK ME ABOUT:</b> {{ facts.judgment[2].ask_me_about }}</p>
      </article>

      <article class="call panel reveal" data-lanes="analytics platform">
        <div class="call-kicker"><span>Call 04</span><span class="dom">trust</span></div>
        <h3 class="call-title">{{ facts.judgment[3].title }}.</h3>
        <p class="call-body">
          An upstream data loss silently broke partner attribution for <strong>$5B+/yr</strong> of revenue — no alert, because the pipeline kept producing plausible numbers. I traced it through <strong>20+ components</strong>, sourced an alternate telemetry feed, and drove <strong>six months of backfills through quarter close</strong> across 7 incidents. Then I rebuilt the thing that let it happen: last-writer-wins became <strong>multi-partner credit</strong>, with validation gates and independent reconciliation against Finance.
        </p>
        <p class="call-out">→ ~$45M/mo recovered and sustained · &lt;1% variance vs Finance · ~80–90% more partner accounts tracked</p>
        <p class="call-ask"><b>ASK ME ABOUT:</b> {{ facts.judgment[3].ask_me_about }}</p>
      </article>

      <article class="call call-wide panel reveal" data-lanes="experimentation platform">
        <div class="call-kicker"><span>Call 05</span><span class="dom">experimentation</span></div>
        <h3 class="call-title">{{ facts.judgment[4].title }}.</h3>
        <p class="call-body">
          The pre-release stress lab ran thousands of simulations per build across <strong>20 workload types</strong>, throwing off ~500 failure signals — far more than a static test plan could triage. The roadmap argued for coverage; the data argued for yield — so I <strong>put multi-armed bandits in charge of picking the next scenario</strong> and tuned scoring thresholds on outcomes, cutting false positives 60% and test-infrastructure cost <strong>40%</strong>. The program came to inform per-build ship / hold calls and helped prevent 10+ top-severity incidents; I led the 2-person effort and wrote the design doc and internal white paper.
        </p>
        <p class="call-out">→ per-build ship / hold calls; 10+ top-severity incidents prevented before rollout</p>
        <p class="call-ask"><b>ASK ME ABOUT:</b> {{ facts.judgment[4].ask_me_about }}</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<hr class="rule"/>

<!-- ============================================================
     §04 — THE RECORD
     Deliberately compact: most readers arrive here holding the
     résumé. Re-rendering it would waste the one scroll they'll give
     us, so this is the spine plus a link to the full document.
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="section-pad" id="record">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="sec-mark">§04 — The record</div>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Nine years of ML that had to <em>earn its keep.</em></h2>
      <p class="sec-sub">
        Mu Sigma → Integral Ad Science → Walmart Labs → Microsoft. The thread: turn
        ambiguity into a system, then verify the system actually moved the number
        it claimed it would. One row per era — the full document is one click away.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="panel ledger-wrap reveal">
      <div class="lt-head">Career ledger — one row per era, one number each</div>
      <table class="ledger-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Years</th><th scope="col">Role / system</th><th scope="col">One number</th><th scope="col"><span aria-hidden="true">§</span><span class="sr-only">Reference</span></th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {%- for row in facts.career_ledger %}
          <tr>
            <td class="lt-years">{{ row.years }}</td>
            <td class="lt-role">{{ row.role }}</td>
            <td class="lt-num">{{ row.number }}</td>
            <td class="lt-ref"><a href="{{ row.ref }}" aria-label="Full record for {{ row.role }}">§</a></td>
          </tr>
          {%- endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="rec panel reveal" id="leadership">
      <div class="rec-head">
        <h3 class="rec-role">Leadership band</h3>
        <span class="rec-co">{{ facts.record[0].company }} · {{ facts.record[0].team if facts.record[0].team else facts.identity.team }}</span>
        <span class="rec-dates">{{ facts.record[0].dates }}</span>
      </div>
      <p class="rec-scope">{{ facts.record[0].scope }}</p>
      <ul class="rec-points">
        {%- for item in facts.record[0].leadership_band %}<li>{{ item }}</li>{% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>

    <p class="edu-line">
      {%- for e in facts.education %}<b>{{ e.degree }}</b> — {{ e.school }} ({{ e.dates }}){% if not loop.last %}<span class="sep">·</span>{% endif %}{% endfor %}
    </p>

    <div class="skills-table panel reveal">
      <div class="skills-row"><span class="k">AI / ML</span><span class="v">{{ facts.skills.ai_ml }}</span></div>
      <div class="skills-row"><span class="k">Tools</span><span class="v">{{ facts.skills.tools }}</span></div>
      <div class="skills-row"><span class="k">Platforms</span><span class="v">{{ facts.skills.platforms }}</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="record-cta reveal">
      <a href="/resume/" class="btn btn-primary" data-goatcounter-click="record-resume-page">The full record — every bullet, every number</a>
      <a href="{{ facts.resume.file }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-ghost" data-goatcounter-click="record-resume-pdf">↓ {{ facts.resume.label }} (PDF)</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<hr class="rule"/>

<!-- ============================================================
     §05 — FIELD NOTES
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="section-pad" id="writing">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="sec-mark">§05 — Field notes</div>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Notes from production, <em>where the demos go to die.</em></h2>
      <p class="sec-sub">
        The gap between the prototype that wows a leadership review and the system
        that survives real engineers trying to break it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="writing-list">
      {%- for w in facts.writing %}
      {%- if w.url %}
      <a href="{{ w.url }}" class="write-row panel reveal">
        <div class="write-when">{{ w.date | humanDate }}</div>
        <div class="write-title">{{ w.title }}</div>
        <span class="write-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/><polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19"/></svg>
        </span>
      </a>
      {%- else %}
      <div class="write-row pending panel reveal">
        <div class="write-when">in queue</div>
        <div class="write-title">{{ w.title }}</div>
        <span class="write-status">{{ w.status }}</span>
      </div>
      {%- endif %}
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     §06 — THE ASK
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="ask" id="ask">
  <div class="wrap-narrow">
    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="sec-mark">§06 — The ask</div>
      <h2 class="ask-title">The evidence rests.<br><em>Your move.</em></h2>
    </div>

    <div class="ask-person reveal">
      <p>
        Hi, I'm <strong>Sarthak</strong>. I lead the design and delivery of the systems this page just walked you through — the agents, the embeddings, the attribution layer Finance reconciles against.
        I'm drawn to problems where the data is ambiguous and the stakes are real, and nine years in the thread is consistent: turn ambiguity into a system, then verify it moved the number it claimed it would.
        Hiring for a <strong>{{ facts.identity.open_to | join(", ") }}</strong>? Email me — I respond fast, and I'll bring the architecture diagrams.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="ask-ctas reveal">
      <a href="mailto:{{ facts.identity.email }}" class="btn btn-primary" data-goatcounter-click="ask-email">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 4h16c1.1 0 2 .9 2 2v12c0 1.1-.9 2-2 2H4c-1.1 0-2-.9-2-2V6c0-1.1.9-2 2-2z"/><polyline points="22,6 12,13 2,6"/></svg>
        {{ facts.identity.email }}
      </a>
      <a href="{{ facts.resume.file }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-ghost" data-goatcounter-click="ask-resume-pdf">↓ Résumé (PDF)</a>
      <a href="{{ facts.identity.linkedin }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-ghost" data-goatcounter-click="ask-linkedin">LinkedIn</a>
      <a href="{{ facts.identity.github }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-ghost" data-goatcounter-click="ask-github">GitHub</a>
      <button class="btn btn-mono copy-btn" type="button" data-goatcounter-click="ask-copy-summary">⧉ copy candidate summary</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script type="text/plain" id="ats-summary">{{ facts.summary.ats | safe }}
Site: {{ facts.meta.site_url }} · Résumé: {{ facts.meta.site_url }}{{ facts.resume.file }} · LinkedIn: {{ facts.identity.linkedin }} · Email: {{ facts.identity.email }}</script>
